+# The USDC balance arc
+
+## TL;DR
+
+`USDC` was never registered as a contract Scaffold-ETH knows about, so
+the hook silently no-op'd. Your teammate registered it in the wrong
+file — a **generated** file that `yarn deploy` rewrites from scratch.
+The right home for a contract your own Hardhat project does **not**
+deploy (a canonical token like USDC) is
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts`, keyed by Base's chain
+id `8453`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Why the hook returned `undefined` silently instead of erroring
+
+`useScaffoldReadContract` doesn't take an address or ABI — you give it a
+`contractName` string and it looks the contract up for you. Under the
+hood it does roughly:
+
+1. `useDeployedContractInfo("USDC")` — resolve name → `{ address, abi }`
+   by looking in the **merged contracts map** (`deployedContracts` +
+   `externalContracts`) for the **current target-network chain id**.
+2. Feed that into wagmi's `useReadContract`, but gated:
+   `query.enabled = Boolean(address && abi && ...args present)`.
+
+When `"USDC"` isn't in the map, step 1 returns `undefined`. So `address`
+and `abi` are `undefined`, `enabled` is `false`, and wagmi **never fires
+the request**. That's exactly the symptom triad you saw:
+
+- **`data` stays `undefined`** — the query is disabled, nothing ever
+  resolves.
+- **No runtime error** — a missing name isn't a thrown exception; the
+  hook is designed to sit in a disabled/loading state, not crash. (Newer
+  SE-2 emits at most a `console.warn`; nothing surfaces in the UI or the
+  network tab.)
+- **No failed request in the network tab** — because no request was ever
+  made. A wrong address would show a reverted RPC call; a *missing name*
+  shows nothing at all.
+
+The lookup is also **chain-scoped**: the contract must exist under the
+chain id of your active `targetNetwork`. Registered under the wrong
+chain id, it's just as invisible.
+
+## 2. Why the teammate's fix worked for a week, then self-destructed
+
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` is a **generated
+artifact**, not a source file. It is overwritten from scratch every time
+you deploy.
+
+Pipeline (hardhat flavor):
+
+```
+yarn deploy
+  → runs packages/hardhat/deploy/*.ts (hardhat-deploy)
+  → writes deployment JSON to packages/hardhat/deployments/<network>/
+  → runs the generate step (scripts/generateTsAbis.ts)
+  → REWRITES packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts
+     from those deployment JSONs
+```
+
+The generator only knows about contracts **your Hardhat project
+deployed** (things in `deployments/`). USDC on Base is a pre-existing
+canonical token — your project never deploys it, so it's never in
+`deployments/`, so the regenerated file can't contain it. Hand-pasting
+the entry survived only until the next `yarn deploy`, which regenerated
+the file and wiped the manual edit. Blank page returns.
+
+It "worked all week" purely because nobody deployed during that week.
+
+## 3. The correct registration
+
+Contracts you reference but do **not** deploy yourself go in the
+**hand-maintained, non-generated** file:
+
+```
+packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+```
+
+Scaffold-ETH merges `externalContracts` with the generated
+`deployedContracts` before every name lookup, and `yarn deploy` never
+touches `externalContracts.ts`. So the entry is durable.
+
+Key it under Base's chain id **`8453`**, and make sure
+`scaffold.config.ts` `targetNetworks` actually includes Base (`chains.base`)
+so the active chain id matches the key.
+
+### The USDC-on-Base entry
+
+Native Circle USDC on Base mainnet:
+`0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913` (6 decimals). It's a proxy,
+but for reads you only need the ERC-20 function fragments in the ABI.
+
+```ts
+// packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+import { GenericContractsDeclaration } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth/contract";
+
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: {
+      address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913",
+      abi: [
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "balanceOf",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [{ name: "account", type: "address" }],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint256" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "decimals",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint8" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "symbol",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "string" }],
+        },
+        // add allowance/transfer/approve if the page needs writes too
+      ],
+    },
+  },
+} as const;
+
+export default externalContracts satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration;
+```
+
+No change needed at the call site — `useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName:
+"USDC", functionName: "balanceOf", args: [connectedAddress] })` resolves
+against the merged map and just works. It survives `yarn deploy` because
+it lives outside the generated file.
+
+### Rendering note
+
+USDC is 6 decimals, not 18. Format with `formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6)`
+(not `formatEther`) or the number will be off by 10^12.
+
+---
+
+## One-line summary
+
+Missing name → disabled query → silent `undefined`; the fix belonged in
+the non-generated `externalContracts.ts` under chain id `8453`, not in
+the deploy-regenerated `deployedContracts.ts`.

